# Fixture bytes are contractual: Git must never rewrite them.
#
# The repository-root .gitattributes sets `* text=auto`, and two fixtures here are
# ASCII text carrying a non-text extension (disguised-script.jpg is PHP source,
# sample-document.pdf is plain PDF syntax). Content auto-detection classifies both
# as text, so a checkout on a CRLF platform (core.autocrlf=true) silently rewrites
# every LF and:
#   - shifts every byte offset in the PDF `xref` table, so the file stops parsing
#     and is no longer the genuinely-parseable document it exists to be;
#   - changes both byte lengths, breaking the declared-versus-actual length check
#     they feed;
#   - breaks every pinned sha256 in ./index.ts, so ensureFixtures() throws for a
#     reason that is not a real defect.
#
# `binary` (-text -diff) disables all conversion and the useless textual diff.
# Patterns are unanchored basenames so they cover ./.generated/ as well, whose
# JPEG, PNG and ZIP artifacts are equally checksum-sensitive. `*.ts` is
# deliberately absent: index.ts is ordinary source and keeps normal text handling.

*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.zip binary
